      "text": "3. Complexity Analysis"
    },
    {
      "type": "complexity_card",
      "timeComplexity": "O(N)",
      "timeExplanation": "We loop through the original array exactly once starting from index 1.",
      "spaceComplexity": "O(1)",
      "spaceExplanation": "No extra memory space is allocated. We reuse the input array directly."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "common-mistakes",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "4. Common Mistakes to Avoid"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "· **Overwriting Original Data**: Since we overwrite the original values, they are permanently lost. If you need the original values later in your program, you must use a separate prefix sum array instead."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "text: · **Out-of-Bounds Indexing**: Starting the loop from `i = 0` will cause accessing `arr[-1]`, leading to program crashes. Always start your loop from `i = 1`."
    },
